                <details class="csm-scoped-keys"><summary>Named connection keys</summary><p>Create a separate code for each workstation or service. Keys expire automatically and can be revoked individually. Site-wide access settings still apply.</p><label for="csm-key-name">Connection name</label><input id="csm-key-name" type="text" maxlength="80" placeholder="Workstation or service"><div class="csm-key-fields"><label for="csm-key-days">Expires after<select id="csm-key-days"><option value="1">1 day</option><option value="7">7 days</option><option value="30" selected>30 days</option><option value="90">90 days</option></select></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="csm-key-write"> Also allow incoming writes</label></div><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-issue-key">Create connection code</button><div id="csm-new-key" hidden><label for="csm-new-code">New private connection code</label><textarea id="csm-new-code" readonly rows="3"></textarea><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-copy-key">Copy new code</button></div><div id="csm-keys"></div></details>
            </section>
            <section aria-labelledby="csm-add-site-title"><h2 id="csm-add-site-title">Add or update a remote site</h2><p id="csm-saved-connection">Save a connection once to use it for both push and pull.</p><label for="csm-remote-name">Connection name (optional)</label><input type="text" id="csm-remote-name" placeholder="Staging or Production" autocomplete="off"><label for="csm-remote-code">Remote connection code</label><textarea id="csm-remote-code" rows="3" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="csm-connect-status"></textarea><p id="csm-connect-status" class="csm-inline-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Paste a complete connection code to connect automatically.</p><p class="csm-connection-help">Copy the code from the remote site’s Trickle page. Check the URL on its first line; the code field clears after saving.</p>
            </section>
            <p class="csm-connection-footer">This site controls both push and pull. The remote site does not need to reach your local address.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <section class="csm-card csm-settings-transfer" aria-labelledby="csm-transfer-settings-title"><div class="csm-panel-body">
        <h2 id="csm-transfer-settings-title">Transfer preferences</h2>
        <p class="csm-note"><label for="csm-transport">Transfer method</label> <select id="csm-transport" aria-describedby="csm-transport-help"><option value="stream" <?php selected($transfer_defaults['transport'], 'stream'); ?>>Automatic (recommended)</option><option value="chunks" <?php selected($transfer_defaults['transport'], 'chunks'); ?>>512 KB chunks</option></select> <span id="csm-transport-help">Continuous downloads, 16 MiB uploads. Both methods resume.</span></p>
        <p class="csm-note"><label><input type="checkbox" id="csm-file-verify" <?php checked($transfer_defaults['file_verify']); ?>> Recalculate plugin and theme checksums</label> — use when files may have changed without their metadata changing. Identical file contents are otherwise skipped using cached checksums.</p>
        <p id="csm-transfer-settings-status" class="csm-inline-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Changes save automatically.</p>
        <h3>Exclusions</h3>
        <p class="csm-note">Always excluded: <code>node_modules</code>, <code>.git</code>, <code>.gitignore</code>, and environment files (<code>.env</code>, <code>.env.*</code>, <code>*.env</code>). Existing destination copies are kept. Git working directories are skipped by default; review any explicit inclusion before preparing.</p>
    </div></section>
        <details class="csm-requirements"><summary>Connection requirements &amp; transfer limits</summary><p>Both sites need this plugin and 64-bit PHP 8.1+, cURL, writable private temporary storage, and writable selected destination files. Production connections require verified HTTPS. Endpoint: <code>?trickle=…</code>; requests use signed <code>X-CSM-*</code> headers.</p><p>Trickle supports single sites and InnoDB tables without foreign keys. It transfers selected plugins, themes, tables and media, not WordPress core or wp-config.php. Destination URLs, Trickle credentials, and cron schedule are preserved. Plugin activation follows the source unless disabled. Database transfers can replace user accounts and other integration settings; keep destination login access and backups available.</p><p>Transfers use retained source snapshots with resumable streaming or 512 KB chunks. Retry resumes at the destination checkpoint. Building the source stream and final staging can still hit hosting time limits; both sites need temporary disk space. Transfers stage privately and validate checksums before applying. The three most recent backups are kept on the destination. Rollback restores the earlier data and will overwrite changes made after applying.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section data-csm-view="diagnostics" aria-label="Diagnostics" <?php if ($view !== 'diagnostics') echo 'hidden'; ?>>
    <details class="csm-card csm-diagnostics" id="csm-diagnostics">
        <summary><span>Diagnostics</span><span class="csm-summary">Connection &amp; transfer log</span></summary>
        <div class="csm-panel-body"><div class="csm-log-toolbar"><p>Recent activity on this site. Logs omit connection keys, request bodies, and database values.</p><div><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-refresh-logs">Refresh log</button><button type="button" class="button" id="csm-download-logs" disabled>Download log</button></div></div><p id="csm-log-status" class="csm-inline-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading recent activity…</p><div class="csm-log-scroll" id="csm-log-entries" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Diagnostic events"></div><p class="csm-log-note">Administrator access is required. Logs are stored outside the public site directory, rotate at 512 KB, and show the latest 200 events. No history is available from before logging was installed.</p></div>
    </details>
